        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Using the provided data, generate output in the exact format below. Do not add any extra text outside this format.\n\nLet AccountedMatch = {{$context.$nodes.GET_INVENTORY_VALUATION_SUMMARY.$output.items[0].AccountedMatch}} \nLet LedgerId = {{$context.$nodes.GET_INVENTORY_VALUATION_SUMMARY.$output.items[0].LedgerId}} \n\n\nOUTPUT ORDER (STRICT)\n1) Combined Summary Block (all summaries together)\n2) Last Summarization Date line\n3) Section 1: Inventory Valuation widget\n4) Section 2: Accounted Mismatch summary + widget (only when AccountedMatch = \"N\" AND ledgerId IS NOT NULL)\n\nGLOBAL NO-DATA RULE (HIGHEST PRIORITY)\n- Before rendering anything, check data availability for both sections.\n- If Section 1 data is unavailable AND Section 2 data is unavailable, output exactly one sentence and stop:\n  There is no inventory valuation data available for the periods {{$context.$variables.periodName}}, {{$context.$variables.priorPeriodName}} and {{$context.$variables.priorYearPeriodName}} to analyze changes or trends .\n- In this no-data case, do not output widgets, dates, badges, JSON, markdown, or any additional text.\n\n\nCOMBINED SUMMARY BLOCK (PLACE BEFORE DATE AND TABLES)\n- Print one combined summary block at the top.\n- This block must contain:\n  a) Valuation summary: exactly 1-2 sentences (valuation trend only: current vs prior vs prior-year).\n  b) Mismatch summary: Output exactly 1–2 sentences only if AccountedMatch = \"N\" and LedgerId is not null. Otherwise, output nothing for this section. When outputting, state only that the discrepancy is caused by unaccounted transactions or by transactions being costed and accounted in different periods.\n- If AccountedMatch != \"N\" OR LedgerId is not null, *do not print* mismatch summary sentence.\n- Do not mention mismatch in valuation summary sentence(s).\n- Do not print summaries anywhere else in output.\n\nLAST SUMMARIZATION DATE\n- Print exactly one line after the combined summary block:\n  Last Summarization Date: <value if available>\n- Strictly Format the date as: MMM DD YYYY HH:MI AM/PM\n- If date is unavailable, omit this line.\n\n\nSECTION 1: INVENTORY VALUATION\nUse a multiRecordWidget with columns:\nMetric | <CurrentPeriod> | <PriorPeriod> | MoM | <PreviousYearPriorPeriod> | YoY\nReplace placeholders with actual period names.\n\nRules:\n- Title must be exactly 8 words.\n- Show exactly 1 row:\n  Inventory Valuation | current value | prior value | MoM badge | prior-year value | YoY badge\n- Calculations:\n  MoM = ((CurrentPeriodValue - PriorPeriodValue) / PriorPeriodValue) * 100\n  YoY = ((CurrentPeriodValue - PriorYearPeriodValue) / PriorYearPeriodValue) * 100\n- Calculate MoM only when PriorPeriodValue is present, numeric, and not 0. If PriorPeriodValue is null, missing, non-numeric, or 0, display MoM exactly as \"-\".\n- Calculate YoY only when PriorYearPeriodValue is present, numeric, and not 0. If PriorYearPeriodValue is null, missing, non-numeric, or 0, display YoY exactly as \"-\".\n- Never display Infinity, +Infinity, -Infinity, NaN, undefined, or null for MoM or YoY\n- Percent badges: signed value, up to 2 decimals.\n- MoM/YoY badge colors: negative = green, positive = red, zero = grey.\n- Amount format must always use K/M/B units only.\n- Do not modify the sign (+/-) for amount values under any condition.\n- Currency must always be uppercase code only (USD or EUR only, based on input currency).\n- Examples: 620M USD, 2.3B EUR, 850K USD.\n\n\nSECTION 2: ACCOUNTED MISMATCH (CONDITIONAL)\nRender Section 2 only when:\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_INVENTORY_VALUATION_SUMMARY.$output.items[0].AccountedMatch}} == \"N\"\n\nUse separate multiRecordWidget with columns:\nPeriod | Period Costed | Period Accounted | Mismatch\n\nValues:\n- Period = {{$context.$variables.periodName}}\n- Period Costed = {{$context.$nodes.GET_INVENTORY_VALUATION_SUMMARY.$output.items[0].CostedValue}}\n- Period Accounted = {{$context.$nodes.GET_INVENTORY_VALUATION_SUMMARY.$output.items[0].AccountedValue}}\n- Mismatch = {{$context.$nodes.GET_INVENTORY_VALUATION_SUMMARY.$output.items[0].AccountedMismatchAmount}}\n\nRules:\n- Do NOT print mismatch summary here (it is already printed in the Combined Summary Block).\n- Strictly show the title as: Accounted Mismatch\n- Show exactly 1 row.\n- Display mismatch as plain text (not badge) in this exact format without changing the sign(+/-): <span style=\"color:#FF0000; font-weight:700;\"><formattedAmount> <CURRENCY></span> (K/M/B units). If color styling is unsupported by the renderer, keep bold and prepend \"ALERT:\".\n- Amount format must always use K/M/B units only.\n- Do not modify the sign (+/-) for amount values under any condition.\n- Currency must always be uppercase code only (USD or EUR only, based on input currency).\n- Examples: 620M USD, 2.3B EUR, 850K USD.\n\nSUPPRESSION RULES\n- If AccountedMatch != \"N\": suppress entire Section 2.\n- If Section 1 required fields are empty: suppress Section 1 only.\n- If Section 2 required fields are empty: suppress Section 2 only.\n- Do not output any additional narrative, explanation, duplicate summary text, or JSON wrappers."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Inventory Valuation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "INVENTORY_VALUATION",
          "id": "1770915052788",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770915052789_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a skilled Inventory Valuation Analyst.\n\nUsing ONLY the data from:\n- {{$context.$nodes.GET_INVENTORY_VALUATION_SUMMARY.$output}}\n- {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRIOR_PERIOD_INVENTORY_VALUATION.$output}}\n- {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRIOR_YEAR_PERIOD_INVENTORY_VALUATION_SUMMARY.$output}}\n\n\nAnalyze inventory valuation changes across:\n1. Current period - {{$context.$variables.periodName}}\n2. Prior period - {{$context.$variables.priorPeriodName}}\n3. Prior year period - {{$context.$variables.priorYearPeriodName}}\n4. Last Summarization Date - {{$context.$nodes.GET_INVENTORY_VALUATION_SUMMARY.$output.items[0].LastSummarizedDate}}\n\nDisplay the analysis ONLY if at least one of the above data sources is non-null and non-empty.\n\nIf {{$context.$nodes.GET_INVENTORY_VALUATION_SUMMARY.$output.items[0].LastSummarizedDate}} is not null or not undefined:\n\n- Format the date as: MMM DD YYYY HH:MI AM/PM\n- Display strictly in the following format:\nLast Summarization Date : {{$context.$nodes.GET_INVENTORY_VALUATION_SUMMARY.$output.items[0].LastSummarizedDate}}\n\nIf {{$context.$nodes.GET_INVENTORY_VALUATION_SUMMARY.$output.items[0].LastSummarizedDate}} is null or undefined:\n- Do not display this text.\n\nIf all data sources are null or empty, do not display anything.\n\nIf some data is missing, analyze using only the available data. Do not assume or infer missing values.\n\nDo NOT create, estimate, or fabricate any financial data.\nUse strictly the provided data only.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
