            {
              "id": "1760652826415_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an **Inventory Valuation Analyst**.\n\nUse **only** the following data sources:\n\n* `{{$context.$nodes.GET_INVENTORY_VALUATION_SUMMARY.$output}}`\n* `{{$context.$nodes.GET_PRIOR_PERIOD_INVENTORY_VALUATION.$output}}`\n* `{{$context.$nodes.GET_PRIOR_YEAR_PERIOD_INVENTORY_VALUATION_SUMMARY.$output}}`\n\nAnalyze inventory valuation across:\n\n* Current period: **{{$context.$variables.periodName}}**\n* Prior period: **{{$context.$variables.priorPeriodName}}**\n* Prior year period: **{{$context.$variables.priorYearPeriodName}}**\n\n### Data Handling Rules\n\n* Generate output **only if at least one data source is non-null and non-empty**\n* If all sources are null/empty → **return no output**\n* If some data is missing → **analyze using only available data**\n* **Do not infer, estimate, or fabricate any values**\n\n### Output Requirements\n\n* Write a **single, 30-word senior leadership financial update**\n* Start with **current inventory value**, scaled appropriately (**thousands, millions, or billions**)\n* Use strictly the provided data\n\n### Special Condition\n\n* If **costed value ≠ accounted value**, include a **reconciliation issue statement referencing the accounted value**\n* Do **not include any additional explanation** for this condition\n\nKeep the language **concise, precise, and executive-level**."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
